WEBVTT

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:11.260
I haven't seen you here in a while.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:13.350
That will be normal until the plan to

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:14.750
increase AHSMB production is under way.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.490
Now then, how is Black 6 doing?

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.320
Display my battle report.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:24.400
High battle capacity, 
but lacks cooperation.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.290
Right.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:28.440
It's a common trait in most of the 
Cosmopolitan Academy students.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:31.530
They are skilled and fully 
realize their elite status.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:32.790
They refuse to cooperate with others,

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.580
tending to look down on them instead.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:38.080
Right... Individually, they 
may be excellent warriors,

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.760
but they are unfit for an army.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.080
Didn't you argue that we should put more

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.400
emphasis on teamwork, even 
if it meant a slight drop

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.840
in their specs, rather than 
pursue individual aptitude?

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.580
In a battle that relies on one hero,

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:52.560
the front will fall apart 
if we lose that hero.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.930
But in the upcoming final battle...

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.350
This happened sooner than expected.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.160
What did?

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.270
The JURIA-System drastically boosts

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:06.310
the pilot's affinity 
with his AHSMB unit.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.320
You're aware of this, aren't you?

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.490
I am...

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:11.250
There is a reason for that.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.210
The AHSMB and pilot are 
created from the same DNA.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:18.090
AHSMB have minds of their own!

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.790
That's ridiculous!

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:22.610
When an AHSMB unit awakens, 
in the worst case scenario,

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:25.380
it could potentially eradicate 
the pilot's personality.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:28.100
The units are that dangerous...?

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.890
We have obtained none other 
than Prometheus' fire.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:35.010
I wonder if we should 
boost its precision.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:37.750
He busted it up pretty bad yet again.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:41.590
We'll lend a hand, so 
let's hurry and fix it up.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:45.190
Our AHSMB just needed 
some basic maintenance.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.340
Thank you!

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.080
With such a strong forward,

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.970
we don't have to worry 
about our support unit!

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:50.880
True enough!

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.140
It'd be pretty bad if the 
support unit got banged up.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.070
Oh, you're here?

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:59.240
This is my team. Of course I'm here!

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:02.500
And we've even got them lending a hand.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.300
Honestly, as long as the pilot is 
okay, we can fix up the unit...

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:11.210
Huh?

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:12.560
Here!

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:13.980
Thanks...

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.940
Don't mention it!

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:18.340
Let's hurry and repair this puppy

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.610
so Izuru can get out 
there and kick more butt!

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:21.750
Right!

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.390
We'll lose respect as mechanics

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.550
if Izuru's unit can't keep up with him!

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:27.320
We've gotta work harder!

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:28.650
It is with help from

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:29.980
behind the scenes that allows

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:30.860
the ace to enter combat.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.290
By Degawa

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.290
Too many syllables.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:40.610
I can't believe I needed saving...

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:47.810
What was that back there?

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:49.530
Dang!

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:53.180
Didn't Izuru's moves totally 
surpass his unit's specs?

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:56.060
His reaction speed went 
0.73 over the limit!

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.300
It's like he moved 
before he could think.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:00.430
What a terrifying thought...

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.920
Isn't that incredible?

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.220
I wonder what my unit'd look like?

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.070
If I pulled that off, would 
the girls be all over me?

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.070
Izuru!

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:10.320
Kei...

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.750
Kei's been worried sick this whole time!

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.830
Really? Sorry to have made you worry.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.330
For you to be so concerned,

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.340
does that mean you have the hots for me?

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:28.260
He's like a beast... Too cool!

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.090
Who, me?

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:32.490
That's not true.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:34.560
What the heck?!

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.590
I'm concerned about two things.

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:40.800
They aren't fatal, are they?

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:43.950
His Harmonic Level is 
still elevated and he is

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:45.610
suffering from horrible fatigue.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:47.480
His Harmonic Level...?

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.910
Right. It looks like that's 
causing his fatigue.

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:55.070
When an AHSMB unit awakens, 
in the worst case scenario,

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:58.130
it could potentially eradicate 
the pilot's personality.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:01.500
Could you give him a 
thorough examination?

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:04.000
Is that an order?

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:05.530
It is!

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.240
All right.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.550
By the way, have you heard about Amane?

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.750
How she got promoted for her 
accomplishments in the Battle of Ceres?

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.850
Reika said we're going to celebrate.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.340
Is that a must?

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:21.010
Consider the situation!

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:22.980
We'd go nuts if we didn't drink.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:29.690
Vesta Base.

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:31.310
With the frontlines 
constantly pullin' back,

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:33.490
this has become the battlefield.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:37.000
But it was supposed to 
be our rear mining base.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:41.070
Hey! At least the bunnies have 
made our job a bit easier.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:43.500
And we'll work kinda hard.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.060
I'm counting on you!

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.140
Lt. Commander Amane, reporting for duty!

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:57.520
Congratulations on your 
promotion to Commander.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:01.580
But I just became a 
Lieutenant Commander...

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:05.140
Additional orders just came in.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:07.010
As of now, you're a Commander.

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:09.740
Why did I get promoted so quickly?

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:13.440
It shows how short we are 
on competent officers.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:16.660
I know you have just arrived, 
but please prepare to depart.

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:18.200
Is it the enemy?

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:19.750
That's right.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.850
The spy satellites around 
our frontline bases

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:23.070
have been destroyed.

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:25.370
It's a clear sign that they're invading.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:26.450
Understood.

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:28.450
Where is the detailed report?

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:31.220
I have already sent it to 
your vessel's database.

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:35.290
None of the satellites

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:38.230
sensed anything until just 
before they were destroyed.

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:39.750
Indeed.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.630
Lacking intel on the enemy forces,

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.340
we cannot afford to mobilize 
the base's main force.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:46.260
I'm counting on you.

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:48.730
Sir! I will set out immediately!

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:57.080
Are you all right?

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:58.740
Yeah!

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:02.330
Drawing manga like always?

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:03.750
Care to take a look?

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:10.670
It's good...

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:19.520
Izuru is acting weird!

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:22.050
Is that really anything new?

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.600
His manga was good!

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:26.520
That IS weird!

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:28.820
Yo! Hangin' in there?

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:29.940
I'm fine!

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.980
Aren't ya acting a bit different?

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:34.850
Who, me?

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:37.390
I'm still me!

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:39.950
True enough...

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:43.520
Then I guess everything's cool.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:45.620
What? Leaving already?

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:49.210
Gotta train! I can't let ya show me up.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:51.960
You've got my back!

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.160
I checked on him.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.560
He really was weird.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:00.890
So are you.

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:02.380
Pickled Squid Guts

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:06.230
He was strangely cool...

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:10.350
No, no, no! There's just no way!

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:11.600
What's wrong?

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:14.890
Well, uh, ummm...

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:16.060
I have some free time.

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:17.200
Maybe I could offer a word of advice.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:20.970
There was this guy I never 
really noticed before,

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:23.810
but now he seems so cool...

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:24.910
What do you think?

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:29.120
Well, could it be the 
Suspension Bridge Effect?

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:30.270
That's it! That!

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:32.660
It's a big theory that some 
psychologists proposed a long time ago!

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:34.730
They conducted experiments 
to see if someone

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:37.970
who was physically excited would 
realize that he was in love!

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.600
Y-you sure know a lot about it.

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:42.670
I actually study stuff 
related to romance.

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:44.940
They said that you notice 
your subconscious feelings

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:48.190
for the person after 
something special happens.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:54.430
No, no, no! This can't possibly be love!

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:56.070
Is there a problem...

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:58.040
Kitty?

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:02.610
This is love!

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:06.460
Yo! What's up?

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:08.080
I came to bring this.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.660
How'd you know that I was out of paper?

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:13.000
Kei told me.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:16.010
Yeah? It isn't easy being popular!

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.560
How is it? Any good?

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:24.340
Yeah, it's goo-

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:27.430
By the way, are you okay?

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:29.890
Of course I'm just fine!

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:32.070
In fact, I almost feel too good.

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:34.930
You get knocked down and 
pop right back up, huh?

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:36.930
Well, I am a hero.

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:39.350
A hero? I suppose so.

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:40.320
I'm counting on you, Hero!

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.300
I'm fighting for you.

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:51.790
No doubt about it! He's weird.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.240
Isn't he?

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:54.710
You're acting weird, too.

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:02.220
They didn't respond until 
after it had been destroyed!

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:06.500
Either they truly are understaffed 
or their staff is incompetent.

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:08.170
I'm getting something on my sensor!

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:10.690
Enemy attack!

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.020
Commence battle!

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:13.150
Roger!

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:29.040
It's good...

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:32.590
A pine?

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:36.340
Potted plants are inauspicious 
in a hospital room!

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:40.390
Hey, Kei! You came to see me?

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:43.320
I brought get-well treats, 
but you might not like them.

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:47.470
If you made them for me, 
anything is awesome.

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:52.390
Izuru, hang in there! Don't die!

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:53.970
May I help you?

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:57.430
Hello? Can you hear me?

00:11:58.310 --> 00:11:59.990
He's unconscious! Airway, clear!

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:02.230
He isn't breathing! I 
need the respirator!

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:03.840
Beginning cardiac massage!

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:05.820
Chest compression! It's ineffective!

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:06.950
Preparing the AED!

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.850
Paddle electrodes, ready!

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:11.330
Analyzing the cardiogram!

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.870
This is going to emit 
a shock, so get back!

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:18.680
Huh? What happened?

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:20.370
He's alive!

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:22.340
Kei, did something happen?

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:25.010
You had me worried.

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:29.630
His Harmonic Level is back to normal?

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:32.670
We're up against a company that is

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:34.370
breaking formation as it draws in.

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:35.770
Make sure to keep your formation

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.340
so individual fighters 
don't break through.

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:38.350
Roger!

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:45.300
Tch! These guys are kinda tough!

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:46.730
They're faster than usual!

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:48.700
Patrick, don't leave my side!

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:53.740
Damn it!

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:55.410
I'm surrounded!

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.750
Their movements seem random, 
but there is a pattern!

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.950
There is an enemy company 
equipped with optical stealth!

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:05.630
They're hiding behind the other 
company while in stealth mode!

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.540
Shoot around the ships that stand out!

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:08.390
Roger!

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.140
It worked! Bull's eye!

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:14.890
Same here!

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:21.930
This is Doberman!

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:25.060
Enemy reinforcements are 
approaching Classified Point 004.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:26.440
Requesting immediate rescue!

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:27.280
I repeat!

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:30.280
Doberman has sent a request 
for emergency rescue!

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:32.620
You are authorized to sortie.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:34.040
Emergency take off!

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:35.110
Roger!

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:37.860
Engines will transfer from idling 
to full drive in 30 seconds.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.590
I've finished inputting 
Navigational Patterns A to N.

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:42.080
Take the fastest route!

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:42.920
Roger!

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.500
Such is the situation.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:52.980
The leader this time 
will be Toshikazu Asagi.

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:54.240
Izuru Hitachi will remain on standby.

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:55.730
I can fight!

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:57.690
Red 5 is still undergoing repairs.

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:00.400
Ange Kuroki will be the forward.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:01.850
Everything else will 
be the same as usual.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:02.610
Roger!

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:10.770
We're too outnumbered... 
We can't even retreat.

00:14:10.770 --> 00:14:12.990
Until reinforcements arrive, preserving 
our forces takes precedence!

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:15.200
At least tell us, "Take them all down!"

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.830
Overconfidence can be dangerous, 
but we should be fine.

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:19.380
This is still within reason!

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:21.700
I'll treat you to dinner 
when you come back.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:22.620
Lucky!

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:25.170
That's a death flag, so don't say that!

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:31.830
If I went out, those enemies would be...

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:38.450
Enemy company sighted!

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:40.450
The target has split into five 
groups and is headed for us!

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:41.260
Their relative speed-

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:42.400
They're here!

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:44.820
What?!

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:46.060
Stealth mode!

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:47.700
My sensors can't read them.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:48.500
Damn it!

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:50.560
Tamaki, fly at full speed and 
break the enemy's formation.

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:52.150
Suruga, offer fire support!

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:53.770
Kei, confirm the enemies' locations!

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:56.150
Ange, widen the hole 
Tamaki's about to make!

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:56.750
Roger!

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.120
Eat this!

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:00.830
They dodged around it?!

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:04.210
That won't work.

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:06.920
Good goin'!

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:08.590
Nice job, Black 6!

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:09.830
Naturally.

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:11.680
I'm doing a good job, too!

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:15.170
I've spotted several enemy fighters!

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:16.640
We're completely surrounded.

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:25.980
You may handle the rest.

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:26.900
Roger!

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:35.780
Damn! You lowly ground beetles!

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:37.120
How dare you?!

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:40.070
Calm down, Ange!

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:41.280
Don't go after them.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.880
Who gave you permission 
to call me by my name?!

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:46.800
That's too dangerous! Pull back.

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:50.080
I don't feel alive after 
all of this hiding!

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:58.800
What happened?

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:00.890
Our radar and all of our sensors 
are functioning properly.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.950
The base is functioning properly.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:04.890
That must have been a lag from 
when we changed power sources.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:05.810
I see...

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:12.070
Is this it?

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:19.750
Commence verifying 
translation and analysis.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:25.450
It isn't here. I must go deeper in.

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:28.990
A firewall?

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:33.130
MJP?

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:37.680
Ange, where are you?

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:39.810
She's completely surrounded!

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:41.980
Damn it! What should I do?

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:51.740
Pleguzesia...

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:53.870
As I had suspected.

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:04.360
Don't do it, Ange! Don't follow them!

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:06.610
What should I do...?

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:09.000
Reinforcements!

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:12.340
Doesn't that lamata look tasty?

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:13.590
Let me have him!

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:15.540
Please, help yourself.

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:17.210
What a hearty feast!

00:17:17.670 --> 00:17:19.010
My fighters are to retreat!

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.230
The enemies are swapping out!

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:29.320
This is our chance!

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:32.110
Suruga, fire at the 
incoming enemy company!

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:33.610
You can count on me!

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.570
Tamaki, fire!

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:37.020
Roger!

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:48.250
Damn nobodies, gettin' 
full of yerselves!

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:51.200
There are several enemy 
fighters around Black 6.

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:53.950
Black 6's armor integrity 
is down by 30%.

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:56.370
Rate of energy consumption is at 22/s.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:57.800
The unit's temperature 
is currently rising!

00:17:58.040 --> 00:17:59.210
This looks bad.

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:02.330
Purple 2, new enemies have 
appeared at Point: Tango!

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:05.980
Blue 1, prioritize rescuing Black 6.

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:07.470
There are too many enemy fighters.

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:08.410
I can't get near him!

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:10.550
It's like I could keep shooting 
and shooting forever!

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:12.950
A second group of enemy fighters 
are approaching from behind!

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:14.320
If only I could send out Red 5...!

00:18:14.930 --> 00:18:16.740
We only have the core up and working!

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:18.410
I'll go in just the core!

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:23.120
I'm heading out!

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:24.320
I thought so!

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:25.500
It's ready to go.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:28.290
We figured this might happen. 
It's ready for action!

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:49.440
Red 5's core, standby: OK!

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:50.900
Routes, all green.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:52.060
Take off, ready.

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:53.360
Blast off!

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:07.780
The only thing you stinkbugs have 
goin' for you are yer numbers!

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:09.710
Move it, pests!

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:13.340
I'm overheating?! Not now!

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:19.790
Just 'cause I can't move...!

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:23.130
Do whatever it takes to clear a path.

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:37.240
Damn it! If only we could 
squeeze in one more attack.

00:19:40.310 --> 00:19:41.320
Izuru?

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:42.270
Guys!

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:45.370
He came in his core?!

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:48.450
Now!

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:49.250
You're in the way!

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:51.170
Finish off that small fry first!

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:04.680
You can't have him!

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:07.390
It changed forms!

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.130
My lamata...!

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.770
Why can't I hit you?!

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:18.230
Of all the little-!

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:18.940
There!

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.280
What?!

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:21.240
And once more!

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:25.740
He's amazing...

00:20:30.150 --> 00:20:31.620
R-retreat!

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:35.790
The enemy company is pulling back.

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:40.530
They're running away...

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:43.620
Ange, did you get hurt?

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:46.220
No...

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.520
I'm glad you're okay!

00:20:57.010 --> 00:20:59.920
He willingly flew into 
the hunting grounds?

00:21:00.560 --> 00:21:05.560
Do the Earthlings act under a different 
set of principles from ours?

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:12.580
Congratulations on 
becoming a Lt. Commander!

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:17.380
Actually, I just got 
promoted to Captain...

00:21:17.620 --> 00:21:18.580
What?!

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.440
What's this? You jumped two ranks?

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:23.080
Amane, did you die in combat?

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:24.620
I'm not dead!

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:25.620
Wait!

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:27.870
You woke up a Lt. Commander and 
you're a Captain by evening?

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:30.590
The GDF must be pretty 
darn understaffed.

00:21:31.170 --> 00:21:34.340
Well, I did go from the General 
Staff Office to the frontlines.

00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:37.030
It will allow me to fight closer 
to where the actual combat is.

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:40.160
We'll be working together 
more often now.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:41.290
Sure will!

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:43.720
Why the long face?

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:46.000
We hardly ever get to 
celebrate, so let's drink up!

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.490
Yep! Drink, drink!

00:21:53.650 --> 00:21:55.330
External access?

00:21:59.700 --> 00:22:02.550
I have finally found our target.

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:06.330
This is our target.

00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:10.090
They refer to this location as the 
Gurantseere Cosmopolitan Academy.

00:23:41.060 --> 00:23:56.080
"Your Hero"
